{"step_index":604,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:02:15Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 3 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. proceed\n2. what aobut horologion.matins and all the other hours? what about all the otyher sections of the book? \n3. start building an implementation plan.\n4. Add page ranges as citations \n5. What was the work that was in progress from the beginning of this chat -- full recap.\n6. Hows it going? Was it determioned what the difference is between these two panels?  Whats next? Whats been accomplished? Whats been hallucinated instead of accomplished? How can you tell?\r\n\n7. We in this chat need to refocus on the Cantor Dashboard. The implementation plan is executed in a separate chat window. Why do we have those two panels there? They are diesplaying almost identical information.\n8. \"Typikon Digest\" part or panel or whatever can be removed in favor of \"Service Digest\" However, when you compaRe both of them actually against the typikon, you can see they are hallucinated and do not refelct the typikal usage. How can we make those two panels one, and then canonically audit their contents against the typikon source file?\n9. Unify the panels first. On front end and back end to reduce any duplications or puling \"same data from different points\" or \"different edatas from same point\" so there is no possible way for the ai to hallucinate conflations\n10. Nothing is loading yet. Begin creating the comprehensive audit implementation plan.\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n### Continuation Summary\n\n---\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n1. **Fix Dashboard Resolution Loading Bug**\n   * **Status**: IMPLEMENTATION\n   * **Context**: When resolving a date (e.g. `08/24/2026`), the dashboard displays a spinning wheel in Liturgical Context, says \"Loading Cantor booklet...\", and does not render. We discovered a lingering reference to `el.digestContent` at line 273 in `cantor_dashboard/main.js` (`el.digestContent.innerHTML = ...`) which throws a TypeError because `digestContent` was removed from the DOM cache when unifying the Reference Panel into `serviceDigestContent`.\n   * **User Phrasing**: *\"Nothing is loading yet. Begin creating the comprehensive audit implementation plan.\"*\n\n2. **Create Comprehensive Canonical Audit Implementation Plan**\n   * **Status**: PLANNING\n   * **Context**: The user instructed us to create a comprehensive implementation plan to canonically audit the generated digest rubrics against the authentic Typikon sources (2010 Lviv Typikon / Dolnytsky Typikon Part II) to eliminate any structural or rubrical hallucinations.\n   * **User Phrasing**: *\"Begin creating the comprehensive audit implementation plan.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n\n* **User Directive (Focus & Scope)**:\n  > *\"We in this chat need to refocus on the Cantor Dashboard. The implementation plan is executed in a separate chat window. Why do we have those two panels there? They are diesplaying almost identical information.\"*\n* **User Directive (UI Unification & Anti-Conflation)**:\n  > *\"Typikon Digest\" part or panel or whatever can be removed in favor of \"Service Digest\" However, when you compaRe both of them actually against the typikon, you can see they are hallucinated and do not refelct the typikal usage. How can we make those two panels one, and then canonically audit their contents against the typikon source file?*\n* **User Directive (Execution Priority)**:\n  > *\"Unify the panels first. On front end and back end to reduce any duplications or puling \"same data from different points\" or \"different edatas from same point\" so there is no possible way for the ai to hallucinate conflations\"*\n* **User Feedback (Live Loading State & Next Step)**:\n  > *\"Nothing is loading yet. Begin creating the comprehensive audit implementation plan.\"* (accompanied by screenshot showing loading spinner).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n\n1. **Decoupled Standalone Calendar Source**:\n   * Updated `RuthenianEngine` in [core.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/core.py) with `calendar_source` parameter and almanac bypass logic.\n   * Updated `/api/resolve` and `/api/roadmap` in [server.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/server.py).\n   * Added the Calendar Source dropdown to [index.html](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/index.html) and [main.js](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/main.js).\n2. **Reorganized Triodion Files**:\n   * Relocated and renamed Triodion files to `assets/text_lenten_triodion.json` and `assets/text_floral_triodion.json` in both Stamford and Royal Doors.\n   * Applied dynamic root path resolution in [parse_triodia.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/parsers/parse_triodia.py).\n3. **Initial Key Standardization**:\n   * Migrated 15 legacy flat keys in `text_horologion.json` and added `LEGACY_KEY_ALIASES` + `db_get` in [text_db.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/text_db.py).\n4. **Reference Panel UI Unification**:\n   * Merged the separate \"Typikon Digest\" and \"Service Digest\" tabs in [index.html](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/index.html) into a single, cohesive **Service Rubrics Digest** panel with the `View Office` dropdown.\n   * Streamlined [main.js](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/main.js) to route all rubric formatting through `renderServiceDigestContent`.\n   * Verified tests: all 379 test suite cases pass, and server endpoint integration tests pass (6 passed in 16.68s).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n\n* **Dashboard Loading Bug Root Cause**:\n  * In `cantor_dashboard/main.js` line 273 (inside `resolveDate` before the `fetch` call), there is a line:\n    `el.digestContent.innerHTML = '<p class=\"placeholder-text\">Loading Typikon instructions...</p>';`\n  * Because we removed `digestContent` from `el`, `el.digestContent` is `undefined`, causing `resolveDate()` to crash immediately on a `TypeError: Cannot set properties of undefined (setting 'innerHTML')` before completing the fetch or clearing the context spinner!\n  * **Fix**: Change line 273 to use `if (el.serviceDigestContent) { el.serviceDigestContent.innerHTML = '...'; }`.\n* **Canonical Typikon Authority**:\n  * The canonical standard is the **2010 Lviv Typikon / Dolnytsky Typikon Part II**.\n  * The engine rubrics are generated via `typikon_digest_generator.py` and `engine/generation.py`, backed by the resolver modules in `engine/resolvers/`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n\n#### Edited Files\n* [index.html](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/index.html): Lines 180–224: Unified Reference Panel into a single `Service Rubrics Digest` with `service-digest-select`.\n* [main.js](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/main.js):\n  * Lines 54–65: Cleaned up element cache `el`.\n  * Lines 209–218: Cleaned up copy button listener.\n  * Lines 303–312: Removed `renderDigestHtml` from `resolveDate`.\n  * Lines 1913–1935: Removed `refTabs` event listeners in `initReferencePanel`.\n* [text_db.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/text_db.py): Defined `LEGACY_KEY_ALIASES` at module level, added `humanize_key()` and `class TextDB` wrapper.\n\n#### Viewed Files\n* [main.js](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/main.js):\n  * Lines 260–340: `resolveDate` and `renderErrorState`.\n  * Lines 760–970: `parseServiceDigest` and `renderServiceDigestContent`.\n* [server.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/server.py): Lines 263–365: `api_resolve` endpoint implementation.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n1. **Immediate Next Step: Fix Line 273 in `cantor_dashboard/main.js`**:\n   * Open [main.js](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/main.js#L273) and replace `el.digestContent.innerHTML = ...` with:\n     ```javascript\n     if (el.serviceDigestContent) {\n         el.serviceDigestContent.innerHTML = '<p class=\"placeholder-text\">Loading Typikon instructions...</p>';\n     }\n     ```\n   * This immediately fixes the dashboard date resolution and allows the Cantor booklet, context badges, and Service Rubrics Digest to load seamlessly.\n\n2. **Second Next Step: Create Comprehensive Audit Implementation Plan**:\n   * Create `implementation_plan.md` in the artifacts directory targeting a full canonical audit of the digest rubrics output against the **2010 Lviv Typikon / Dolnytsky Typikon Part II**.\n   * Define benchmark dates (Ordinary Sunday, Sunday + Polyeleos Saint, Great Feast, Lenten Weekday).\n   * Cross-reference each generated section against `docs/encyclopedia/master_citation_matrix.md` and the 20 canonical paradigms.\n   * Send the plan to DeepSeek via `scripts/perfect_plan_via_deepseek.py` to perfect it and present it to the user.\n\n**Customization files read**:\n* `.agents/AGENTS.md` (Enforcing compliance, Rule 6 Evidence Gate, Rule 11/12 Checklists).\n* `.agents/references/anti_patterns.md` (Zero-tolerance anti-pattern check).\n\nYou have the 12 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787611593633]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/.user_uploaded/media_1787611593633.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-24T22:47:19Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787611800226]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/.user_uploaded/media_1787611800226.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-24T22:50:58Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787611816371]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/.user_uploaded/media_1787611816371.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-24T22:50:58Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787611816377]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/.user_uploaded/media_1787611816377.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-24T22:50:58Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787612518661]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/.user_uploaded/media_1787612518661.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-24T23:02:12Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-07-20T01:00:11Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media__1784507162777]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/media__1784507162777.png\nLast Edited: 2026-07-20T00:26:05Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media__1784507330614]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/media__1784507330614.png\nLast Edited: 2026-07-20T00:28:59Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: print_keys]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/scratch/print_keys.py\nLast Edited: 2026-07-20T00:52:09Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: rename_json_keys]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/augus/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40