{"step_index":611,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:02:28Z","content":"I will create the comprehensive canonical audit implementation plan in `implementation_plan.md`.","thinking":"**Begin Audit Planning**\n\nI've fixed all the date-related JavaScript errors! The dashboard should be error-free regarding dates. I'm now starting to draft the comprehensive audit implementation plan.\n\n\n**Defining Audit Scope**\n\nI've defined the audit's scope: a plan to check the digest generator against the 2010 Lviv and Dolnytsky Typikons, identifying rubrical errors and inconsistencies. I've established the audit's canonical grounding, referencing *Ordo Celebrationis*, Dolnytsky, and the 2010 Lviv Typikon. I'm focusing on the twenty canonical paradigms for the audit's dimensions.\n\n\n**Detailing Audit Metrics**\n\nI've established the second audit dimension: office-by-office rubrics and choreography. For Vespers, I'm noting Kathisma determination, stichera count ratios, Dogmatikon selection rules, and triggers for Litiya and Artoklasia. Matins focuses on \"God is the Lord\" vs. \"Alleluia,\" Kathismata rotation, the Polyeleos, and Canon odes, along with the Doxology. I'm checking Hours' cycling and Liturgy's Antiphon selection and entrance sequences.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Comprehensive Canonical Typikon Source Audit Implementation Plan.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"<!-- [GENERATOR: Gemini 3.7 Flash] -->\n# Implementation Plan — Comprehensive Canonical Typikon Source Audit\n\nThis implementation plan establishes the methodology, benchmark test suite, and correction pipeline to canonically audit the Typikon Coded digest generator and engine resolvers against the **2010 Lviv Typikon** and the **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Objective & Canonical Authority Hierarchy\n\nThe objective is to eliminate all rubrical hallucinations, erroneous hymn distribution ratios, and structural discrepancies in the generated Service Rubrics Digest, ensuring 100% fidelity to canonical Ruthenian/UGCC liturgical usage.\n\n### Hierarchy of Authority (Rule 2):\n1. **Ordo Celebrationis** (Rome, 1944 / 1996) — Primary rubrical standard for service choreography.\n2. **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V** (Lviv, 1899) — Detailed rubrics for the daily cycle, Menaion, Triodion, and Pentecostarion.\n3. **2010 Lviv Typikon** — The authoritative modern UGCC codification.\n4. **Liturgicon & Horologion** — Verbatim prayers, litanies, and ordos.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scope of the Canonical Audit\n\nThe audit covers all six core liturgical dimensions across the 20 Canonical Paradigms:\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    Canonical Audit Dimensions & Checkpoints                  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Vespers Architecture                                                      │\n│    • Kathisma assignment (Saturday evening Kathisma 1; Weekday Kathisma cycle)│\n│    • Stichera at \"Lord, I Call\" (Total count 10, 8, 6, 4; exact source ratios)│\n│    • Doxastikon & Theotokion/Dogmatikon selection (Saturday Tone Dogmatikon) │\n│    • Litiya & Artoklasia inclusion rules (Rank 5 Polyeleos / Rank 6 Vigil)   │\n│    • Aposticha hymn distribution & Sunday Theotokion matching                │\n│    • Dismissal Troparia chain (Resurrectional -> Saint -> Theotokion)        │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. Matins Architecture                                                       │\n│    • Hexapsalmos & opening doxology sequence                                 │\n│    • \"God is the Lord\" vs. \"Alleluia\" (Simple Lenten / Requiem distinction)  │\n│    • Kathismata & Sessional Hymns (Kathisma 2/3 + Sedalen with Theotokion)   │\n│    • Polyeleos, Megalynarion, & Evlogitaria insertion                        │\n│    • Hypakoe & Anavathmoi (Gradual hymns of the Tone)                        │\n│    • Matins Gospel & Eothinon cycle connection (Resurrection Gospel #1-11)   │\n│    • Canon Ode stacks (Odes 1–9 ratios) & Seasonal Katavasia assignment      │\n│    • Praises Stichera distribution (Counts of 8, 6, 4 + Glory/Both now)     │\n│    • Doxology Type (Great Chanted vs. Small Read) based on feast rank        │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. Hours Architecture                                                        │\n│    • Troparia / Kontakia rotation matrix across 1st, 3rd, 6th, and 9th Hours │\n│    • Lenten Hours vs. Ordinary Hours (Kathisma insertions, Ephrem bows)      │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. Divine Liturgy Architecture                                               │\n│    • Antiphons selection (Daily Psalms vs. Typika & Beatitudes vs. Festal)   │\n│    • Little Entrance Troparia & Kontakia combination order (Temple, Feast,   │\n│      Sunday, Patron, Saint, Steadfast Protectress)                           │\n│    • Prokeimena & Alleluia double-reading precedence rules                   │\n│    • Epistle & Gospel pericope sequencing (Lucan/Johannine/Matthean jump)    │\n│    • Kinonikon (Communion Verse) precedence                                  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 5. Combined & Vesperal Liturgies                                             │\n│    • Presanctified Liturgy structure & Old Testament readings (Genesis/Prov) │\n│    • Holy Thursday, Holy Saturday, Nativity Eve, Theophany Eve structures    │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 6. Fasting & Vestments                                                       │\n│    • Canonical fasting degree (Strict, Wine/Oil, Fish, Fast-free)            │\n│    • Vestment color mapping based on liturgical season and feast classification│\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Benchmark Audit Suite (Representative Dates)\n\nWe will construct a canonical benchmark matrix testing every unique rubrical collision:\n\n| Case ID | Benchmark Date | Liturgical Condition | Canonical Citation |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **BENCH_01** | Octoechos Sunday (Tone 7) | Ordinary Sunday with Simple Saint (Rank 1/2) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. II, Ch. 1–2; *Ordo* §§ 25–55 |\n| **BENCH_02** | July 6, 2026 | Sunday colliding with Polyeleos Saint (St. Sisoes / St. Athanasius) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. III, July 6; *Ordo* §§ 60–68 |\n| **BENCH_03** | August 6, 2026 | Transfiguration of the Lord (Great Feast of the Lord) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. III, Aug 6; *Ordo* §§ 80–92 |\n| **BENCH_04** | August 15, 2026 | Dormition of the Theotokos (Great Feast of the Theotokos) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. III, Aug 15; *Ordo* §§ 93–105 |\n| **BENCH_05** | Clean Monday 2026 | Great Lent Day 1 (Alleluia, Great Compline, Ephrem Bows) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. IV, Triodion Clean Week |\n| **BENCH_06** | Wednesday Wk 4 Lent | Liturgy of the Presanctified Gifts | *Dolnytsky* Pt. IV, Presanctified Ordo |\n| **BENCH_07** | Holy Saturday 2026 | Vesperal Liturgy of St. Basil (15 OT Readings, White Vestments) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. IV, Holy Saturday |\n| **BENCH_08** | Thomas Sunday 2026 | Renewal Sunday (Pentecostarion Feast of the Lord) | *Dolnytsky* Pt. V, Thomas Sunday |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Implementation Steps & Evidence Gates\n\n### Step 4.1: Automated Benchmark Extractor Script\nCreate `scripts/audit_canonical_digest.py` to:\n* Run the engine for each benchmark date.\n* Generate the complete Service Rubrics Digest.\n* Output structured JSON comparison artifacts to `tests/benchmarks/`.\n\n### Step 4.2: Canonical Discrepancy Matrix\n* Cross-examine generated digests against the verified 2010 Lviv Typikon text.\n* Catalog every discrepancy (e.g. inverted Troparia order, missing Dogmatikon, wrong Katavasia season).\n\n### Step 4.3: Resolver Rectification\n* Apply precise rubrical fixes directly to the engine resolver modules:\n  - [vespers.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/resolvers/vespers.py)\n  - [matins.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/resolvers/matins.py)\n  - [liturgy.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/resolvers/liturgy.py)\n  - [hours.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/resolvers/hours.py)\n  - [generation.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/engine/generation.py)\n\n### Step 4.4: Automated Test Gate & Regression Hardening\n* Integrate all audited benchmark cases into `tests/test_canonical_audit_truth.py`.\n* Ensure 100% green test passes across all 379+ test suites.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verification Plan\n\n### Automated Test Commands:\n```powershell\n# 1. Run Session Compliance\n$env:PYTHONPATH=\".\" ; .venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_session_compliance.py -v\n\n# 2. Run Canonical Audit Suite\n$env:PYTHONPATH=\".\" ; .venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest tests/test_canonical_audit_truth.py -v\n\n# 3. Run Full Test Suite (excluding UI readability)\n$env:PYTHONPATH=\".\" ; $env:PAGER=\"cat\" ; .venv\\Scripts\\python -m pytest --ignore=tests/test_ui_readability.py --verbose\n```\n","Description":"Create Comprehensive Canonical Typikon Source Audit Implementation Plan","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\augus\\/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/implementation_plan.md","toolAction":"Writing implementation plan for canonical audit","toolSummary":"Writing implementation_plan.md"}}]}
