ines [Y-Z]\r\n28: \r\n29: #### Step 1: Locate Orders\r\n30: - [ ] Find \"ORDER OF [SERVICE]\" header\r\n31: - [ ] Note exact line numbers\r\n32: \r\n33: #### Step 2: Extract Elements (Variant 1: [TYPE])\r\n34: | # | Element | Typikon Line | Current JSON | Status |\r\n35: |:-:|:--------|:-------------|:-------------|:-------|\r\n36: | 1 | | | | |\r\n37: \r\n38: #### Step 3: Extract Elements (Variant 2: [TYPE])\r\n39: | # | Element | Typikon Line | Current JSON | Status |\r\n40: |:-:|:--------|:-------------|:-------------|:-------|\r\n41: | 1 | | | | |\r\n42: \r\n43: #### Step 4: Cross-Reference Part II (Paradigms)\r\n44: - [ ] Check paradigms affecting this service\r\n45: - [ ] Note 2-saint stacking rules\r\n46: \r\n47: #### Step 5: Verify Implementation\r\n48: - [ ] All elements have JSON representation\r\n49: - [ ] All variable elements have resolve functions\r\n50: - [ ] No definitional gaps (false positives)\r\n51: \r\n52: #### Step 6: Implement Gaps\r\n53: - [ ] Add missing hooks\r\n54: - [ ] Add Typikon citations to rubrics\r\n55: - [ ] Validate JSON\r\n56: \r\n57: #### Step 7: Create Stress Tests\r\n58: - [ ] 2-saint scenario\r\n59: - [ ] Feast + saint collision\r\n60: - [ ] Seasonal override (Lent, Pascha)\r\n61: ```\r\n62: \r\n63: ---\r\n64: \r\n65: ## Quick Reference: Key Typikon Sections\r\n66: \r\n67: | Section | Content | Audit Priority |\r\n68: |:--------|:--------|:---------------|\r\n69: | Part I: Orders | Service structures | HIGH |\r\n70: | Part II: Paradigms | 20 stacking rules | HIGH |\r\n71: | Part III: Menaion | Fixed feast rubrics | MEDIUM |\r\n72: | Part IV: Triodion | Lenten/Paschal overrides | HIGH |\r\n73: | Part V: Temple | Temple feast rules | LOW |\r\n74: | Footnotes | Exception clarifications | AS NEEDED |\r\n75: \r\n76: ---\r\n77: \r\n78: ## Maximum Liturgical Day (Stress Test Baseline)\r\n79: \r\n80: Per Dolnytsky Part II Line 31:\r\n81: > **\"The ecclesiastical rubric does NOT provide for more than TWO services to saints [on one day].\"**\r\n82: \r\n83: | Scenario | Components | Complexity |\r\n84: |:---------|:-----------|:-----------|\r\n85: | Sunday + 2 Saints | Resurrection + 2 Menaion | MAX |\r\n86: | Great Feast + Saint | Feast dominates | HIGH |\r\n87: | Forefeast + 2 Saints | e.g., November 2 | HIGH |\r\n88: | Lenten Weekday + Saint | Triodion + Menaion | MEDIUM |\r\n89: | Afterfeast + Apodosis + 2 Saints | Ultimate edge case | EXTREME |\r\n90: \r\n91: ---\r\n92: \r\n93: ## Replication Instructions for Other Models\r\n94: \r\n95: 1. **Start with typikon_search_methodology.md** — Follow 7 steps exactly\r\n96: 2. **Use this template** — Copy audit checklist for each service\r\n97: 3. **Reference matins_variants_gap_matrix.md** — Pattern for element comparison\r\n98: 4. **Apply to struct JSON files** — Add missing elements with Typikon citations\r\n99: 5. **Validate JSON** — `py -c \"import json; json.load(open(file))\"`\r\n100: 6. **Update task.md** — Track progress per service\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
